114
00:05:36,010 --> 00:05:40,950
Alright, in today's Fluency Builder, we have a number of phrases you could use in a small talk situation.

115
00:05:41,350 --> 00:05:42,270
The first one's a question.

116
00:05:43,390 --> 00:05:44,410
How's the family?

117
00:05:45,400 --> 00:05:46,000
How's the family?

118
00:05:46,600 --> 00:05:50,560
Now, it's how apostrophe s the family, right?

119
00:05:50,700 --> 00:05:53,840
So how is the family would be the extended way of saying it.

120
00:05:54,080 --> 00:05:54,200
That's right.

121
00:05:54,320 --> 00:05:55,980
But this is a short way to say it.

122
00:05:56,140 --> 00:05:56,800
It's very common.

123
00:05:57,160 --> 00:06:06,410
And you normally say this with people who are a little bit older, people who have kids. So I haven't seen you in a long time, Marco, and I know you have some kids and I can say, how's the family?

124
00:06:07,120 --> 00:06:07,610
How's the family?

125
00:06:07,810 --> 00:06:07,990
That's right.

126
00:06:08,450 --> 00:06:16,550
And it's actually, it may seem strange the way that this sentence is made, but it's very, very much similar to how are you?

127
00:06:16,890 --> 00:06:19,030
You have how to be and you in the subject.

128
00:06:19,480 --> 00:06:23,030
That's right. And this is a very polite way to say hi. How are you?

129
00:06:23,390 --> 00:06:24,290
How is your family?

130
00:06:25,000 --> 00:06:25,570
How is the wife?

131
00:06:27,130 --> 00:06:27,590
How's the wife?

132
00:06:28,050 --> 00:06:29,550
And she said, well, you know what?

133
00:06:29,690 --> 00:06:30,410
Everything is great.

134
00:06:30,830 --> 00:06:31,230
I'm fine.

135
00:06:31,550 --> 00:06:35,400
And Jack's, I guess that's her husband, is doing well.

136
00:06:35,940 --> 00:06:39,820
Jack is doing well. So doing well, thanks. This means good.

137
00:06:40,580 --> 00:06:44,100
Okay. But you know, when we say the answer to this question, how are you?

138
00:06:44,300 --> 00:06:45,060
I'm well.

139
00:06:45,680 --> 00:06:47,400
That's the correct answer.

140
00:06:47,860 --> 00:06:49,240
I'm good is not correct.

141
00:06:49,720 --> 00:06:49,880
Right.

142
00:06:50,400 --> 00:06:53,800
So if somebody says, how are you? You can say, I'm well.

143
00:06:54,440 --> 00:06:55,680
Or you can say, I'm doing well.

144
00:06:56,220 --> 00:06:57,400
That's a positive answer.

145
00:06:57,540 --> 00:06:58,520
Things are going well.

146
00:06:59,240 --> 00:07:00,720
You could say, not so well.

147
00:07:01,040 --> 00:07:03,470
That's not a, not, not, not good things are happening.

148
00:07:03,980 --> 00:07:04,270
Very good.

149
00:07:04,430 --> 00:07:06,450
And it's very important to point out the difference.

150
00:07:06,710 --> 00:07:10,850
As Catherine said, you don't, you don't, you shouldn't use good.

151
00:07:11,250 --> 00:07:13,030
I'm doing good or I'm good.

152
00:07:13,670 --> 00:07:18,910
Yeah, no, it's incorrect because good is an adjective and we're, we're looking for an adverb here.

153
00:07:19,440 --> 00:07:19,610
That's right.

154
00:07:20,440 --> 00:07:21,440
Well.

155
00:07:21,440 --> 00:07:22,270
That's correct. All right.

156
00:07:22,470 --> 00:07:27,530
And to finish things off, Mr. Campbell and Michelle were headed, headed the same way.

157
00:07:27,930 --> 00:07:30,370
So they decided to share a taxi.

158
00:07:32,080 --> 00:07:38,440
That's right. So to share a taxi means two people or three people will pay for one taxi together.

159
00:07:39,120 --> 00:07:43,300
So maybe Marco, I see you on the street and I know that you have to go to a conference.

160
00:07:43,660 --> 00:07:44,940
I'm going to the same conference.

161
00:07:45,400 --> 00:07:46,700
Let's share a taxi.

162
00:07:47,000 --> 00:07:48,080
It will cost less.

163
00:07:48,840 --> 00:07:49,060
That's right.

164
00:07:49,320 --> 00:07:53,220
So you will share the cost between all the people in the cab.

165
00:07:53,580 --> 00:07:58,000
Now there's another way of saying it as well. More common, I think in the, in the United States.

166
00:07:58,800 --> 00:07:58,920
That's right.

167
00:07:59,100 --> 00:08:00,480
We say split a taxi.

168
00:08:00,860 --> 00:08:02,400
Let's split a cab.

169
00:08:03,360 --> 00:08:03,740
Split a cab.

170
00:08:04,100 --> 00:08:06,100
Now remember that it's a taxi cab.

171
00:08:06,820 --> 00:08:08,600
So sometimes people just don't say taxi.

172
00:08:08,760 --> 00:08:09,220
They say a cab.

173
00:08:09,480 --> 00:08:10,140
Let's split a cab.

174
00:08:10,360 --> 00:08:11,360
Let's share a cab.

175
00:08:11,740 --> 00:08:13,860
That's right. Cab, taxi, both are okay.

176
00:08:14,500 --> 00:08:15,680
All right. Very good.

177
